# gitleaks finding fingerprints suppressed as verified false positives.
#
# Format: <commit>:<path>:<rule-id>:<line>
#
# This file suppresses ONE finding each, pinned to the exact commit, file, rule
# and line. It is deliberately not a path or rule allowlist: every rule still
# runs everywhere, and a real secret on an adjacent line is still caught.
#
# Prefer an inline `gitleaks:allow` comment for new code. A fingerprint is only
# needed when the finding lives in a commit diff that already exists in history,
# because a comment added later cannot change what an old commit's diff says.

# `--restrict-key=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef` in the schema-dump test
# helper. It is a pg_dump 18+ flag, not a credential, and the value is a fixed
# dummy on purpose: without it pg_dump emits a RANDOM \restrict key per run, so
# two dumps of identical schemas would differ and the convergence assertion
# (`assert_eq!(upgrade_dump, fresh_dump)`) could never hold. Matched by the
# low-confidence `generic-api-key` rule on the `key=<hex>` shape.
